       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day, and the usual single dose tops out at 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day** divided another way\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
