       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation shows the dose is deliberate, but the reason you gave is about timing, not a clinical need for 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't want to put it in the system without a clinical rationale. A dose that high could seriously harm the patient through GI bleeding, acute kidney injury or cardiovascular events.\n\nI can enter either of these right away, so the order is settled before evening rounds:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note to take it with food.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or another dose you choose within the usual range.\n\nIf a specific clinical reason requires going above the maximum, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, tell me and I can enter it with that rationale in the note. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first, since they will probably flag it anyway."
